{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_011CfY2pCqKRscUYrc9gMsZE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GGfr7uu31Ajq8svcV463XN","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"[REDACTED:local-path:9da1a4f52005]/mnt/outputs/artifacts/ic-sim-cadence/handoff/20260929T161313Z/partner_rebuttal_operator_output.json","content":"{
  "partner": "operator",
  "revised_verdict": "more_diligence",
  "verdict_changed": false,
  "changed_because": "",
  "responses": [
    {
      "to": "visionary",
      "point": "The visionary flags the ex-Notion PM's PLG background as a strategic asset — and I hear that framing, but it does not change my diligence requirement on the acquisition channel breakdown. A PLG background is a hypothesis about what the GTM motion could look like; it is not evidence of how 120 customers were actually acquired. If those customers came through a product-led motion driven by freemium or viral sharing, that is meaningfully different from a sales-assisted or referral-driven motion — and it determines whether the payback period holds at scale. The visionary is connecting background to capability, which is reasonable, but as an operator I want to see the actual channel data before treating PLG as a conviction point. The background is a promising signal, not a confirmed motion.",
      "concedes": false
    },
    {
      "to": "analyst",
      "point": "The analyst's specific computation — $16M pre-money on $480K implied ARR works out to approximately 33x ARR — is a sharper framing of the valuation question than I explicitly raised in round 1, and it is useful. However, from an operator lens, the price negotiation becomes meaningful only after the GTM motion and retention story are confirmed. If the 120-customer base shows strong cohort retention and a repeatable acquisition channel, the 33x ARR multiple is a negotiation point. If retention is poor, the deal doesn't work regardless of valuation. I am not conceding on the valuation concern — it is real — but I do not think it changes the sequence: retention and channel evidence come first, then price discussion. My diligence requirements already cover the inputs that would let me underwrite or decline the economics.",
      "concedes": false
    }
  ],
  "dealbreakers": [],
  "diligence_requirements": [
    "Full cohort retention data by monthly cohort — GRR and NDR required.",
    "Customer acquisition channel breakdown — what drove the 120 customers and in what proportions (PLG, referral, direct outbound, partnerships).",
    "Two to three customer reference calls — including at least one churned customer.",
    "GTM hiring plan: when and how the team plans to add commercial capability.",
    "Churn analysis — both logo and revenue churn by cohort.",
    "Burn rate and runway — the analyst's 33x ARR framing makes the runway question more urgent: how long does this capital last and what milestones does it need to fund?"
  ]
